WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.750
Speaker 1: Trump 2024 may be dying before
it even starts in multiple new 2024 Republican

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:08.750
polls.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:15.400
Ron DeSantis is leading Donald Trump, and
this is before Trump makes his big announcement

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.690
tonight, which we will talk about in a moment.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.449
There are two arguments about the importance
of this, which we will talk about in a moment.

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:28.580
First and foremost, there is a YouGov America
poll, and it asked Republicans, do you prefer

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.060
DeSantis or Trump in 2024?

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.670
Republicans and Republican leaners say 42%.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.329
Ron DeSantis 35%.

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:42.410
Donald Trump 10% neither.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.560
13%.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.560
Not sure.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.489
Now the neither and the not sure could make
the difference and push it back to Trump.

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:56.120
But we are now for the first time getting
these types of numbers.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:03.320
This poll was conducted November 9 to 11,
meaning it was after the 2022 midterm, and

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:08.630
indeed it would be a logical causation to
infer, although for now we can say it's a

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:16.729
correlation, it could be a causation that
Trump's controversial and sort of like contested

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:20.050
endorsements in 2022 that went bad.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:24.950
That includes Carrie Lake, although we didn't
know about that until yesterday, Mehmet Oz,

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:31.690
Doug Mastriano, etc., that the failure of
those endorsements has reinvigorated support

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.229
for someone other than Trump.

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:37.869
Now you might say, Well, David served with
total respect and tears in my eyes.

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:39.509
That's only one poll.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:44.590
Well, there are now multiple polls that show
DeSantis leading.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:49.159
Yes, there's a new morning consult poll in
which Trump is still winning.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:57.729
However, we now have a CWC Research poll in
Texas which shows Texas prefers DeSantis over

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:00.010
Trump 43 to 32.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.390
That's a pretty big deal.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:07.000
We have a Georgia Republican primary poll
from WPA intelligence which shows DeSantis

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.369
plus 20 over Trump.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:13.590
We have one in Florida which shows DeSantis
plus 26 over Trump.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.590
New Hampshire.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:15.700
DeSantis plus 15.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.400
Iowa, DeSantis plus 11.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.440
And one from the Association for Canadian
Studies for a general national primary, which

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.450
shows DeSantis plus two.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.140
This splits.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.830
This changed right after November 8th.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.960
Now, there's two arguments here.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:35.960
Argument.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.810
One is that this is all completely irrelevant.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.099
The argument that it's irrelevant is.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:51.440
If you actually have Trump and DeSantis running
an ugly, contested, snippy primary against

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:58.600
each other, Trump will do the same sort of
stuff that he did in 2016, making fun of people,

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:03.830
ridiculing them, being Teflon, and that ultimately
DeSantis isn't going to be able to do it and

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.159
that DeSantis is going to fall off.

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:09.739
There are some major differences, however.

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:11.500
Number one.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:17.420
If indeed this is a two candidate race, Trump
versus DeSantis, that's very different than

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:21.980
what would have happened than what did happen
in 2015 and 2016, which was you had 18 candidates

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.190
or 19 candidates to start with.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:29.530
You had a lot of these ones and twos people
polling one and 2%, and Trump just would stick

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.890
it out long enough for one of the ones and
twos to fall off.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:38.110
And Trump picks up a point, and then another
one of the ones and twos falls off and Trump

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.849
picks up another point or two.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:42.750
There was this attrition sort of dynamic.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:49.689
If you just start with really just two candidates
in 2024, Trump and DeSantis, with Trump being

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:54.470
a known political entity, with Trump already
being president, with Trump already losing

00:03:54.470 --> 00:04:01.159
himself in 2020 and hurting Republicans in
22, you can argue the circumstances are so

00:04:01.159 --> 00:04:06.019
different that it is not going to be a similar
situation.

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:10.530
But for the first time, the betting markets
now pointing to DeSantis over Trump in the

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:16.049
primary and increasingly polling pointing
to DeSantis over Trump.

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:49.100
Tonight is the big announcement.

